# Line endings are stated here rather than left to each contributor's
# core.autocrlf setting.
#
# The repository already stores LF throughout -- this is not repairing damage.
# It makes that a property of the repo instead of a coincidence: a contributor
# with core.autocrlf unset or false, editing on Windows, would otherwise commit
# CRLF, and a shell script whose shebang reads "#!/bin/sh\r" cannot be executed
# on macOS or Linux (the kernel treats the carriage return as part of the
# interpreter path and reports "bad interpreter").
#
# LF everywhere, including .ps1: PowerShell reads LF without complaint, and one
# rule is easier to keep true than two. Working copies on Windows are unaffected
# -- Git Bash, PowerShell and Python all read LF happily.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gz binary
*.zip binary
